{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Shoelace_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Shoelace Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Determinant)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Determinant)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Cross_Product)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Cross Product)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangle in the coordinate plane has vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7b5b0f6bc744edb5062deb4a05371b3748a621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(\\log_21,\\log_22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/4068083dd12c0b0f7323ee3f5785920c27acad4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(\\log_23,\\log_24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acafe012c9a5b5ba03fa740de8c2d35a2cc6675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(\\log_27,\\log_28)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b54066a76ca0c280ed116d6f031a5f59dfaf239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\log_2\\frac{\\sqrt3}7\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\log_2\\frac3{\\sqrt7}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\log_2\\frac7{\\sqrt3}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\log_2\\frac{11}{\\sqrt7}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\log_2\\frac{11}{\\sqrt3}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"669\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Shoelace_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Shoelace_Theorem)\">Solution 1 (Shoelace Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Shoelace Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We rewrite:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64abd2a5b1d71a4064909a2682a4607591ef22c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b88d50fe2460eca8da02b272e844084fa4806f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(\\log _{2} 3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf54b09c2ebb9618717973aeb2e7a0dcf21d8e3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(\\log _{2} 7, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>From here we setup Shoelace Theorem and obtain:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1182de865af3acd7d76494533b36c199da1e47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(2(\\log _{2} 3) - log _{2} 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Following log properties and simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f103bd6f865857ad5310e168be21076823d139a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\log_2 \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"113\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~MendenhallIsBald, ShortPeopleFartalot\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Determinant.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Determinant)\">Solution 2 (Determinant)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Determinant)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To calculate the area of a triangle formed by three points \\( A(x_1, y_1) \\), \\( B(x_2, y_2) \\), and \\( C(x_3, y_3) \\) on a Cartesian coordinate plane, you can use the following formula:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25bd42e0a783077028a3464eb3e6dba400bf005.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\\]\" width=\"387\" height=\"37\" />\nThe coordinates are:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/4743e45f36fc247b2ceabcaefe9370476851c851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b706413ecc73ecb95ad0d1a2c58336c748497ced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(\\log_2 3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a048f2ac6ff84b4f918da2fe99abfb645431f21a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(\\log_2 7, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Taking a numerical value into account:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72040c1667c3faece7458868ae2345f3acfe74b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 \\cdot (2 - 3) + \\log_2 3 \\cdot (3 - 1) + \\log_2 7 \\cdot (1 - 2) \\right|\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"37\" />\nSimplify:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e77d1541bedfed028dfca6cf59bf1a9cae17cb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + \\log_2 3 \\cdot 2 + \\log_2 7 \\cdot (-1) \\right|\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4247b37364ccac9c511eed62d8a1d937661822d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\log_2 (3^2) - \\log_2 7 \\right|\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/98862491678c122f9f9ce04df28f9393c0a70ce8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\log_2 \\frac{9}{7} \\right|\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" />\nThus, the area is:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/1297c9db4606a8848d84ef43918344fdb87c30f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\log_2 \\frac{9}{7} \\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"45\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f103bd6f865857ad5310e168be21076823d139a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\log_2 \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"113\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Athmyx\">Athmyx</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Geometry)\">Solution 3 (Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_12B_2024_Problem15.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"None\"><img alt=\"None\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/90/AMC_12B_2024_Problem15.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"345\" height=\"288\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>In the graph above, the biggest triangle has legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c00e23bddfc5c5cb4f0793d51b1e29d5e2c7d0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Its area is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c00e23bddfc5c5cb4f0793d51b1e29d5e2c7d0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThere are 3 smaller shapes as well:\n</p><p><br />\n1. Triangle 1. Legs = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975cc685f50f4e7569ff4af547c7a2883418967d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e27ca4bba5f6584534f1b3442639484449b2644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2 3 = \\log_2 \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"38\" />.;\n</p><p><br />\n2. Triangle 2. Legs = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a64ec85864ad508567961661bc3bb3b254cf07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2\\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f50bc417f7f3bb41fa73fa528c38a278b62c638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2 \\frac{7}{3} = \\log_2 \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"151\" height=\"48\" />;\n</p><p><br />\n3. Rectangle. Legs = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a64ec85864ad508567961661bc3bb3b254cf07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2\\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a64ec85864ad508567961661bc3bb3b254cf07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2\\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />.;\n</p><p><br />\nThe area of the triangle is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a66dca7c6b1b5bb1154129feb0e7a4418ea34e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2 7 - \\log_2 \\sqrt{3} - \\log_2 \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}} - \\log_2\\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"279\" height=\"48\" />.\nThis is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/759da4a8c139cd0d1fd98f1d46a63f1627fbd61d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2 7*\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}*\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}*\\frac{3}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"166\" height=\"48\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/82997e11b6995f109778ab8a4b0cb471033811fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\log_2 \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"107\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>~mathwizard123123\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Cross_Product.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Cross_Product)\">Solution 4 (Cross Product)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Cross Product)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area is half of the cross product between two of the vectors. These will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d367c61ca9f528e305ecf371cd4dd0f01804a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[log_2 3, 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f053751df8569d49c95e856bd5e3e3266c60180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[log_2 7, 2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. The cross product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/95314091305a165dc1ccc0bf6ecfe6664ed377ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 log_2 3 - log_2 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, and half of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/82997e11b6995f109778ab8a4b0cb471033811fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\log_2 \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"107\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>~vaishnav\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jyupN3dT2yY&amp;t=0s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jyupN3dT2yY&amp;t=0s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&